Description: Self-hosted IaC + portfolio platform CLI
 BytePort is a self-hosted Infrastructure-as-Code deployment + portfolio
 platform for developer projects. Define one manifest (`odin.nvms`) at your
 repo root and BytePort provisions a MicroVM-backed deployment (via the
 `nvms` Spin runtime), registers the resulting endpoints with a portfolio
 site, and uses an LLM to generate showcase metadata for each project.
 .
 This package ships the `byteport` command-line client which drives the
 manifest engine, manages local deploys, and surfaces diagnostics — all on
 top of `odin.nvms` as the single source of truth. The graphical desktop
 shell is shipped separately via the Tauri `.deb` / `.AppImage` under
 `frontend/web/src-tauri/`.
 .
 Security highlights: AES-256-CFB for secrets at rest, Argon2id for
 password hashing, PASETO v2 for session tokens, SSRF-safe HTTP client for
 user-supplied URLs. Traces exportable via OpenTelemetry.
 .
